    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=\\frac{1}{16},\\quad b=\\frac{3}{16}$",
      "worked": "The probabilities sum to $1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}a+\\frac18+b+\\frac14+\\frac38&=1\\\\a+b&=\\frac14\\qquad\\text{(1)}\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $E(X)=\\sum xP(x)=3.75$:\n$$\\begin{align*}a+2\\left(\\frac18\\right)+3b+4\\left(\\frac14\\right)+5\\left(\\frac38\\right)&=\\frac{15}{4}\\\\a+3b&=\\frac58\\qquad\\text{(2)}\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract (1) from (2):\n$$\\begin{align*}2b&=\\frac38\\\\b&=\\frac{3}{16}\\\\a&=\\frac14-\\frac{3}{16}\\\\a&=\\frac{1}{16}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
